     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Competitiveness of at least 250 Youth and Women among productive but under-served informal sector in business and trade with a focus on AfCFTA enhanced
2.Innovative Financing schemes rolled out for improved productivity and trade competitiveness to at least 200 MSMEs; Expand the work we started under the SDGIF.
3.Support to the Implementation of the National Africa Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA) Implementation Strategy and Action Plan - National and subnational institutional capacity relevant to AfCFTA strategy supported for immediate benefits to accrue to targeted women and youth enhanced.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	AfCFTA awareness Session reached 200 particpants
&#x2022; Sense Making session - Reached about 50 participant with about 90 percent women ( 10 MSMEs to be supported to enhance, build capacity and increase its productivity)
&#x2022; Export trade training ( 350 participant )
&#x2022; Support an online trading platform to assit in arket and trading of the MSMEs products - parternship with Tambula to support the about 30 MSMEs
&#x2022; SDGIF window 4 supporting MSMEs in (Renewable energy , manufacturing and Agriculture) intent to support atleast 10 MSMEs. Actual MSMEs supported to be estabilished.
&#x2022; Sense Making session - Reached about 50 participant with about 90 percent women ( 10 MSMEs to be supported to enhance, build capacity and increase its productivity)
&#x2022; Youth and Women dialogue and advocacy platforms around AfCFTA &#x2013;National Youth Connect Platform with the Ministry of Youth has been estabilished ;
&#x2022; Simplifying the AfCFTA Agreement &#x2013; consultancy Firm has been supported to develop value chain and provide export training to women and youth (350 participants). 
4 series of AfCFTA awareness sessions has been created , and production of Trade/Export Booklets by Namibia Trade forum.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
